  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sri Sathish vs State Of Karnataka on 22 January, 2026 Author: Shivashankar Amarannavar Bench: Shivashankar Amarannavar -1- Nc: 2026:Khc:3574 Crl.P No. 16188 of 2025 Hc-Kar In The High Court Of Karnataka At Bengaluru Dated This The 22Nd Day Of January, 2026 Before The Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Shivashankar Amarannavar Criminal Petition No. 16188 Of 2025 (438(Cr.PC) / 482(Bnss)) Between: 1. Sri Sathish Aged About 48 Years S/O Puttaswamy Gowda Mallenahalli Village Chikkamgaluru District - 577 101. ...Petitioner (By Sri Jagadeesha K J, Advocate) And: 1. State Of Karnataka By Chikkamagaluru Rural P S Rep. By Spp High Court Building Digitally signed by Bengaluru - 01. Lakshminarayana ...Respondent Murthy Rajashri Location: High Court Of (By Sri Harish Ganapathy, Hcgp) Karnataka",
    "facts": "This petition is filed by accused No. 1 under Section 482 of BNSS praying to grant anticipatory bail in crime No. 360/2025 of Chikkamagaluru Rural Police Station registered for offences under Sections 3 and 7 of Essential Commodities Act, 1955 and Sections 3 and 4 of Gas Supply Act (LPG Act Regulation and Supply Distribution Order 2000), 1939 and Section 287 of BNS. Said cylinders were stored in public place and it affects the safety of the persons residing in and around the said place. Petitioner is required for custodial interrogation. With this he prayed to reject the petition. Food Inspector had received credible information and went to the house of the petitioner and found stored 30 cylinders and at that time wife of the petitioner was present. Said 30 cylinders have been seized and they belong to HP, Indane, Bharat companies and include commercial and domestic cylinders. Said cylinders have been seized under mahazar.",
    "arguments": "2. Heard Learned counsel for petitioner and Learned HCGP for respondent - State. 3. Learned counsel for petitioner would contend that the offences alleged against the petitioner are not punishable either with death or imprisonment for life. Maximum sentence that can be imposed for offences NC: 2026:KHC:3574 HC-KAR alleged against the petitioner is imprisonment which may extend to 7 years. Cylinders have already been seized. Petitioner undertakes to cooperate with the Police in the investigation and abide by any conditions to be imposed by this Court. There are no criminal antecedents of the petitioner. With this he prayed to allow the petition. 4. Per contra learned HCGP would contend that total 30 cylinders have been seized from the premises of the petitioner. Out of them, 16 were filled and 14 were empty cylinders.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "2. Heard Learned counsel for petitioner and Learned HCGP for respondent - State. 3. Learned counsel for petitioner would contend that the offences alleged against the petitioner are not punishable either with death or imprisonment for life. Maximum sentence that can be imposed for offences NC: 2026:KHC:3574 HC-KAR alleged against the petitioner is imprisonment which may extend to 7 years. Cylinders have already been seized. Petitioner undertakes to cooperate with the Police in the investigation and abide by any conditions to be imposed by this Court. There are no criminal antecedents of the petitioner. With this he prayed to allow the petition. 4. Per contra learned HCGP would contend that total 30 cylinders have been seized from the premises of the petitioner. Out of them, 16 were filled and 14 were empty cylinders.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
